Matrix trellis packing, procedural codebooks, tensor-core lane ordering and
Hadamard conventions are adapted from quant/pack.cu, quant/frac.cu,
quant/codebook.cuh, quant/exl3_dq.cuh, quant/hadamard_inner.cuh and
modules/quant/exl3_lib/quantize.py. Modifications provide per-lane ring
window decoding into row-blocked FP32 GEMM tiles, the scalar generic ring
decoder as a test-only reference, BF16 operator input/output, FP32 transforms
and accumulation, expert-grouped whole-expert routing, caller-owned scratch
and vLLM native registration.

Compressed n-gram ring mapping and mul1 constants are adapted from
modules/quant/exl3_lib/ngram_codec.py. Modifications provide allocation-free
selected-row decoding, integer-bit layouts, global-row/head ownership masks
and BF16 output after separately rounded FP32 scale multiplication and bias
addition.

The original runtime is not a dependency. No external vLLM integration is
included. Original grants and modification notices are also retained in the
adapted source headers.

